{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline","id":255162,"title":"Has everyone checked out the Demon Storytellers Guide outline?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-12T03:33:30-07:00","id":255162,"title":"Has everyone checked out the Demon Storytellers Guide outline?","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> So while trying to find out why I suddenly couldn't get to the forum, I stumbled upon this page: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-demon-storytellers-guide-open-development/</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> I was surprised no one started a topic about it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> So I guess I'll get the ball rolling.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> I hope there is a lucid dead equivalent for exiles, either in the angel section or the &quot;different hells&quot; section, since becoming an angel again and still being a person is a stated integrator ambition.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> The three shards look interesting, the biblical fantasy has already been mentioned in this forum, the other two are cyberpunk (Deus Ex meets Bladerunner is the short description) and a rather out of left field post apocalypse hack in which the demon PCs dream of a post apocalypse world in which the various masquerades fell but the monsters won, leaving ragged bunch of human survivors seeking to avoid the predation of the supernatural, but when the demons dream this apocalypse world damage and aether use rollover so after a bad day a demon might not have much aether to confront the apocalypse with, or end up dying in their dreams. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> The cyberpunk shard has the players being the god-machine's supersoldiers, stigmatics augmented to enable exploit and embed use, tasked with &quot;retiring&quot; fallen angels. I don't know about anyone else, but I'd through in stuff from heirs to hell by having the &quot;retired&quot; demons being harvested to grow hellblooded to hunt down their own aunts and uncles.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T08:48:49-07:00","id":255339,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of good stuff in there. Almost too much to talk about.<br /> <br /> I'm excited about Giants In The Earth, I'm amused by the SOE, and indifferent towards the apocalypse scenario. And on that note, I wonder if we'll ever get a second Infinite Macabre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T09:18:08-07:00","id":255349,"title":"","content":"This looks incredibly good. Especially how the antagonists of other lines might be presented in Demon and other concepts (what Mummy's judges are to the God Machine maybe). The Biblical setting might be very interesting, maybe Sodom and Gomorrah got literally nuked by some Elimination Structure in Mount Sinai!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T15:28:01-07:00","id":255619,"title":"","content":"I feel the addition of anything crossover related would just steal word count from where it could really be useful. I hope those tidbits are really more blurbs than anything else. So long as they don't drag on like Chapter one of FoH did it could be fine. I'd like to the Observers/ Analysts get expanded upon and maybe even their own set of embeds. Most of the outline sounds okay though. Fingers crossed the writers give the Seraphim attention in the angel section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T15:31:45-07:00","id":255621,"title":"","content":"I guarantee that some of those REDACTEDs refer to qashmallim, and that's the thing I'm most excited to hear about; I've wanted to hear about The Principle in Demon terms since before release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T15:48:13-07:00","id":255624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=255619#post255619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the addition of anything crossover related would just steal word count from where it could really be useful. I hope those tidbits are really more blurbs than anything else. So long as they don't drag on like Chapter one of FoH did it could be fine. I'd like to the Observers/ Analysts get expanded upon and maybe even their own set of embeds. Most of the outline sounds okay though. Fingers crossed the writers give the Seraphim attention in the angel section.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's handy for those of us who like to run crossover heavy games. Even if my PCs aren't cross-splat, the setting elements I use are often from multiple nWoD gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T15:53:26-07:00","id":255627,"title":"","content":"The Biblical setting... I so, so, so want. I need it. Like I was hoping Dark Eras to do it but this is just as good. Can't wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T16:04:09-07:00","id":255630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=255621#post255621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guarantee that some of those REDACTEDs refer to qashmallim, and that's the thing I'm most excited to hear about; I've wanted to hear about The Principle in Demon terms since before release.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guarantee you they don't.<br /> <br /> EDIT:Well, okay, one probably does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-12-2014, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T16:24:37-07:00","id":255651,"title":"","content":"I wish every game-line would put out a book that said, &quot;This is the crossover chapter.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because here's the thing: it doesn't have to be <i>crossover</i>. No one has a problem with having a bunch of story seeds and plot hooks in supplements, and that's all the 'crossover' info is. If you have no intention of running a Demon game mixed with a Vampire PC, then just look at that section and say, &quot;Oh, okay. The God-machine created blood-sucking Exiles that my Demon PCs must contend with. Now what?&quot; You don't have to think about how they mix with Promethean PCs, but rather, &quot;Oh, okay. The God-machine is building an artificial human. What does that mean for my Demon PCs?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T16:44:10-07:00","id":255657,"title":"","content":"True.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">characters.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T17:11:32-07:00","id":255668,"title":"","content":"I'm reserving Judgement on the biblical setting. That has to be written just right, one of my favorite things about Demon was it avoided being legitimately biblical. I've never been offended by a WoD book before, but I had an English Teacher who said &quot;Good literature is supposed to offend you&quot;. Though if the whole thing Usurps...You know this is gonna go a real bad way.<br /> <br /> Also off topic, OP just needs to make a big book of Crossover so it doesn't keep leaking into everything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T20:17:03-07:00","id":255763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=255619#post255619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to the Observers/ Analysts get expanded upon and <b>maybe even their own set of embeds.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That would be an astonishingly fast way to destroy half the point of the Incarnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T20:19:38-07:00","id":255764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=255668#post255668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reserving Judgement on the biblical setting. That has to be written just right, one of my favorite things about Demon was it avoided being legitimately biblical. I've never been offended by a WoD book before, but I had an English Teacher who said &quot;Good literature is supposed to offend you&quot;. Though if the whole thing Usurps...You know this is gonna go a real bad way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me. OWoD Time of Judgement book offended the hell out of me. (Especially the one with the girl and the gargoyle)<br /> <br /> OWoD God is whole lot more of an asshole than God-Machine.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T22:44:37-07:00","id":255851,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the crossover section will address more generic inhabitants of the world of darkness that just happen to interact more with the other inhabitants like spirits and ghosts or relics. <br /> <br /> Anyway, the cyberpunk shard got me thinking &quot;Why isn't Demon already a cyberpunk game?&quot; <br /> <br /> Wouldn't providing its thralls with next gen technology when the world of darkness already has clones, robots, transgenics, and undead cyborgs according to promethean, skinchangers, and antagonists be easier than arranging magic from technology infrastructure? <br /> <br /> Demon can already have the social elements what with demons avoiding Big Brother on steroids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T08:29:21-07:00","id":256070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=255851#post255851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I wonder if the crossover section will address more generic inhabitants of the world of darkness that just happen to interact more with the other inhabitants like spirits and ghosts or relics.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the cyberpunk shard got me thinking &quot;Why isn't Demon already a cyberpunk game?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean it isn't?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=255851#post255851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't providing its thralls with next gen technology when the world of darkness already has clones, robots, transgenics, and undead cyborgs according to promethean, skinchangers, and antagonists be easier than arranging magic from technology infrastructure?</div> </div> </div> </div>So... Gadgets?<br /> <br /> keep in mind, occult physics <i>are </i>the next, next gen of technology. They're the secret laws of reality, which allow you to accomplish things beyond the ken of human sciences. That old, lame quote of &quot;indistinguishable from magic&quot; applies here. So when you're turning people into stigmatics, installing gadgets into them, giving them gadgets and teaching them to do all sorts of crazy shit via occult physics, that's what you're doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T11:45:49-07:00","id":256175,"title":"","content":"Looking at it, I really am excited about the 'urban legends' section. <br /> <br /> I expect this to have a lot of cool ideas to work with as well as good insight into the Demon's hopes and fears. Most urban legends can be traced back to some societal or cultural fear, so it could be good insight into the Demon's psychology.<br /> <br /> It would be fun merging this into actual urban legends, such as bloody mary -- maybe she's a part of an important ritual in the occult matrix...A way to give blood to oil the 'Gears of the world'. However, this sacrifice must be willing and the individual must call it upon themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T22:28:19-07:00","id":256526,"title":"","content":"The Angel section is going to get a lot of use in my game, especially the G-M specific Numina.<br /> <br /> The part that has me the most terrified/excited is the Cipher section. Terrified, because they've taken so long to finally get this part of the setting right. Excited, because they took Matt M. and turned him loose on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T18:24:31-07:00","id":256930,"title":"","content":"I hope that a big name demon like Asmodeus, as well as the Satan Signal, make it into urban legends. The hints at it from the beginning have made me super excited. That, solid examples of Hell, the Biblical setting.. I am extremely eager to get this supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T00:44:47-07:00","id":257030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=256070#post256070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You mean it isn't?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So... Gadgets?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">keep in mind, occult physics <i>are </i>the next, next gen of technology. They're the secret laws of reality, which allow you to accomplish things beyond the ken of human sciences. That old, lame quote of &quot;indistinguishable from magic&quot; applies here. So when you're turning people into stigmatics, installing gadgets into them, giving them gadgets and teaching them to do all sorts of crazy shit via occult physics, that's what you're doing.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Yes, I mean it isn't just like it isn't a biblical fantasy or post apocalyptic which is why they are writing hacks to make demon those things. :</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> You apparently missed my freaking point, so let me reiterate it for you:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Why the hell does the god-machine limit itself to current known technology and post singularity technomagic when it should have every technological stage inbetween at its disposal when there are already mundane groups who are more advanced than current known technology? </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> If the god-machine has either the power to rewrite the laws of physics or knows the laws of physics so well that it knows all the loopholes, then it should certainly be able to come up with clones, chimeras, undead cyborgs, and next gen weapons like valkyrie without resorting to the rube goldberg-esque shenanigans that infrastructure requires. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> So why is the god-machine dependent on infrastructure when it could be making use of next gen but perfectly mundane technology? </span></span></span><br /> <br /> Higher technology is used because it's better, supposedly, not just because, so why is the god-machine not using the best tools for the job? Why isn't the god-machine mass producing weapons that cause Aether to blow up? TFV could do it, and it wouldn't be immediately apparent to demons or further empower them by generating aether, or require essence.<br /> <br /> There are no circumstances in which it makes sense for the united states government to have better toys than the god-machine but as written that's the case.<br /> <br /> Putting in gasoline or plugging something into a wall socket is better than being dependent on human sacrifice to keep something working. <br /> <br /> Mass production is more convenient than one of a kind prototypes, but at infrastructure level things are so complicated mass production doesn't seem possible. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T03:25:08-07:00","id":257152,"title":"","content":"TFV don't exist in Demon by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T07:19:43-07:00","id":257258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=257030#post257030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So why is the god-machine dependent on infrastructure when it could be making use of next gen but perfectly mundane technology?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Two things.<br /> <br /> 1) Arcane Physics. The God Machine is working the world over into it's grand scheme, and it's using principles we simply don't get. Some of those call for inferior tech, but can accomplish more than any amount of high end tech could.<br /> <br /> 2) Stealth. The God-Machine prefers to be unnoticed when possible. It's use of infrastructure is more elegant for that purpose than straight up using next gen tech. I mean, are you going to investiagte a horse shed, or something looks like it came out of college students innovation folder?<br /> <br /> 'Cause the God-Machine is totally behind the horse shed.<br /> <br /> Final note:<br /> <br /> The God Machine can set up a reality computer in that horse shed, where brushing the horse the right ways is the keyboard for local reality.<br /> <br /> When you can do stuff like that, fancy tech stuff seems a bit of a shame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T07:58:55-07:00","id":257265,"title":"","content":"I'm VERY disapinted that there won't be any <b>WoD: Inferno</b> specific crossover info. Game called <b>Demon</b> should have at least some ideas to run with literal Hell Realm. And Satan or Asmodeus should be menitoned at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T08:09:43-07:00","id":257272,"title":"","content":"Wyrd, your disappointment that demons aren't red-skinned horny bastards with pitchforks is well known. You can stop, <i>we know</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-15-2014, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T08:47:29-07:00","id":257298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=257265#post257265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm VERY disapinted that there won't be any <b>WoD: Inferno</b> specific crossover info. Game called <b>Demon</b> should have at least some ideas to run with <u>literal Hell Realm.</u> And Satan or Asmodeus should be menitoned at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the outline:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-demon-storytellers-guide-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/nowshaddap.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> I implore you to cultivate an actual attempt at understanding content. Demonstrably incorrect and thoroughly avoidable is not a good combination of qualities to have tagging one's erroneous statements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T09:07:21-07:00","id":257315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=257298#post257298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-demon-storytellers-guide-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/nowshaddap.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> I implore you to cultivate an actual attempt at understanding content. Demonstrably incorrect and thoroughly avoidable is not a good combination of qualities to have tagging one's erroneous statements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read it on first look, week ago. Implied text has nothing to <b>Inferno</b> and Demon Princes or Diaboli. Rose Baily confirmed it in comments. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T13:33:59-07:00","id":257556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've read it on first look, week ago. Implied text has nothing to <b>Inferno</b> and Demon Princes or Diaboli. </div> </div> </div>You missed some words from your original post, so it's not clear whether you're disapointed that there's no relationship between Demons and the Inferno, or whether you're disappointed there are no Hell realms in a more general sense.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not at all bothered. Demon is it's own bizarre techgnostic monstrosity, aesthetically it just doesn't gel with Inferno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T13:47:18-07:00","id":257561,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure WyrdHamster is sad that the crossover chapter doesn't have any suggestions for crossing Demon with WoD Inferno; something that the highlighted text does not disprove Satchel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T14:05:49-07:00","id":257593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=257556#post257556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You missed some words from your original post, so it's not clear whether you're disapointed that there's no relationship between Demons and the Inferno, or whether you're disappointed there are no Hell realms in a more general sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also it's a literal copy-paste of his post from the comments section of the blog entry, where Hawthorn has already made a cogent response vis-a-vis thematic focuses and Rose has already noted the matter of wordcount. <i>Eight other gamelines</i> is already a bit of a strain without throwing on another two that barely have single complete books' worth of published material to draw from.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Raven, you do realize that, barring the rare and seemingly random instances where my Ignore List doesn't work, I cannot and do not care to engage in conversation with you, yes?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T17:11:51-07:00","id":257697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=256930#post256930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that a big name demon like Asmodeus, as well as the Satan Signal, make it into urban legends. The hints at it from the beginning have made me super excited. That, solid examples of Hell, the Biblical setting.. I am extremely eager to get this supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. I think demon has an amazing concept, but stil lacks of some great details to make the setting more interesting, like famous demons and a historical setting to illustrate how GM operates in different eras. <br /> <br /> I hope we will get some insight, perhaps in the form of legends, about how GM was created. Not a definitive answer, but at least a few options. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T19:13:54-07:00","id":257766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fiction: All the Little Children (.75k)</span></b></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This is a story about a Tempter who believes he\u2019s found his Hell -- a perfect little suburb in the vein of Disney\u2019s vision for Celebration or maybe just </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Stepford Wives</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">. We see how perfect it is... and then we see what he has to do to keep it going, to keep his family safe and to keep his little bubble free of the Machine\u2019s influence.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I hope they go easy on the GrimDark. This fiction looks interesting, but the idea that achieving Hell must end in misery and pain is rarely satisfying for players. Oh, victory should <i>take</i> misery and pain, but at the end of the day, the Descent has to be worth fighting for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T06:27:09-07:00","id":258070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=257556#post257556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm not at all bothered. Demon is it's own bizarre techgnostic monstrosity, aesthetically it just doesn't gel with Inferno.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the posts like this<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=256930#post256930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that a big name demon like Asmodeus, as well as the Satan Signal, make it into urban legends. The hints at it from the beginning have made me super excited. That, solid examples of Hell, the Biblical setting.. I am extremely eager to get this supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>or <b>Amadeu</b>'s one it comes people ARE looking for <b>WoD Inferno</b> stuff, only not knowing they want it. For those that don't know <b>Inferno</b> is &quot;more mysterious biblical Hell&quot; of nWoD, with popcultural demons from <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Exorcist, Omen </span></span></i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">or </span></span><i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Exorsicm of Emily Rose </span></span></i>- and all alike. They are govern by great ones like Amon, Asmodeus, Beelzebub, Belphegor, Leviathan, Lucifer and<br /> Mammon. And best of best - <b>any</b> ephemeral being ( ghost, spirit, astral being and a like ) can become Inferno demons - God-Machine's angels probably also can become <b>Inferno</b>'s demons. If any one looks for &quot;general, mortal&quot; setting things - great stuff and read!<br /> <br /> It would be such pitty gameline called <b>Demon</b> wouldn't at least mentioned <b>Inferno</b> in crossover sections.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=257556#post257556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You missed some words from your original post, so it's not clear whether you're disapointed that there's no relationship between Demons and the Inferno, or whether you're disappointed there are no Hell realms in a more general sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a a bit happy we get Unchained Hell-Hells. But crossover stuff with <b>Inferno</b> would be golden.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Eight other gamelines</i> is already a bit of a strain without throwing on another two that barely have single complete books' worth of published material to draw from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing now there will be Biblical setting and Urban Legend section, Asmodeus here, Leviathan there is all that is needed and small frame on beginning of crossover chapter that states &quot;We couldn't put <b>WoD Inferno</b> full crossover support, but Infernal Host is marked throught whole book. Just look for the signs of literal <b>Inferno</b>'s influence in it.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-16-2014, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T07:45:41-07:00","id":258143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WyrdHamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be such pitty gameline called <b>Demon</b> wouldn't at least mentioned <b>Inferno</b> in crossover sections.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be because Descent has better things to do.<br /> <br /> No. I'm not kidding. Descent has it's own little world to build up. The fact it's getting a crossover chapter is astounding, but space is space, and the sales figures points to the most profitable subjects to cover, that being the other game lines. You could try and add more, but it comes back to the fact that Descent has it's own little world to build. Why waste time on another book of demons when you not only can do so much with the demons you already have, but that you <i>have</i> to do so much with the demons you already have because that's the point of the product?<br /> <br /> And on top of that, why redirect to another book about demons? What, are we saying we need to talk about the Unchained and their relationships with the demons of Pandemonium, the Abyss, and goetic demons too? You <i>could</i> try to argue about how that'snot a bad idea, but then you cross over into the realm absurd.<br /> <br /> Focusing on Inferno is just kind of a bad choice overall. White Wolf made those sort of mistakes in the past with other products, and they've learned from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T08:37:46-07:00","id":258179,"title":"","content":"There isn't really much thematic overlap between the Descent and the stuff in Inferno. Although both use ideas taken from the Judeo-Christian notion of Demons, one is the gnostic 'cast out by the father' version from late pre-Roman Judaism and post-enlightenment Christianity and the other is Medieval folktale 'evil lying spirit' stuff. The kind of stories you would be exploring are quite different and probably as dissimilar as the Descent and another splat like Vampire. (Although I could be wrong here.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T08:46:06-07:00","id":258187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=258143#post258143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Focusing on Inferno is just kind of a bad choice overall. White Wolf made those sort of mistakes in the past with other products, and they've learned from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not focusing - mentioning. If there are Biblical stuff in the book in general, it will lead to &quot;bad press&quot; none the less. It doesn't matter it will be &quot;first demons were fallen angles and made Niphilims&quot; in compared to &quot;Old Testament demons are faught from time to time&quot;.<br /> <br /> If there will be talk about spirits, goetic demons, abyssal demons and Fae demons - I don't see why shouldn't be mentioned one paragraph on Inferno demons ( and some classical, badass demons names few times in the book, even without the stats). Especially as <b>Inferno</b> <i>was</i> mentioned in corebook, in one senatce, but was.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=258179#post258179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't really much thematic overlap between the Descent and the stuff in Inferno. Although both use ideas taken from the Judeo-Christian notion of Demons, one is the gnostic 'cast out by the father' version from late pre-Roman Judaism and post-enlightenment Christianity and the other is Medieval folktale 'evil lying spirit' stuff. The kind of stories you would be exploring are quite different and probably as dissimilar as the Descent and another splat like Vampire. (Although I could be wrong here.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that <b>Descent</b> demons have much more in common with <b>Inferno</b> demons, than with spirits of <b>Werewolf</b>, <b>Changling</b> demons, or vampires themselves, <i>because</i> they have at least some common origin and elements - like both are perfect liars, &quot;possessing&quot; humans, combat with God(Machine), &quot;free&quot; will, demonic forms, cults of worshipers. Not to compare even to alien &quot;demons&quot; of <b>Mage</b> line, that are &quot;demons&quot; only because they are strange ( and good with that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> Really, much interesting overlap, even if aesthetics are in clash here somehow. MUCH more than any other gameline. ( Even if <b>Inferno</b> is just one book ).</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-16-2014, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T14:47:18-07:00","id":258476,"title":"","content":"Arguably, the biggest reason to do actual gamelines instead of <i>Inferno</i> is that they have more content attached to each of them, so finding a way to connect them actually gives a Demon storyteller more material to work with than <i>Inferno</i>'s single book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T15:04:48-07:00","id":258486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=258187#post258187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[SIZE=12px]<br /> <br /> I would argue that <b>Descent</b> demons have much more in common with <b>Inferno</b> demons, than with spirits of <b>Werewolf</b>, <b>Changling</b> demons, or vampires themselves, <i>because</i> they have at least some common origin and elements - like both are perfect liars, &quot;possessing&quot; humans, combat with God(Machine), &quot;free&quot; will, demonic forms, cults of worshipers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coming back from a self-imposed silence until I'm done with my September exams just to say that, actually, Werewolf's spirits (especially the bad ones that serve the Maeljin) have all that and even more and have arguably more in common with Inferno demons than the Descent ones, which, aside from the Asmodeus in there (which is a special case by design) are slaves to their own sinful nature and have not that much when it comes to &quot;real&quot; free will. I really can't guess what made you believe the contrary, honestly.<br /> <br /> Also, Demon the Fallen is an awesome game and has everything you're looking for. Only speaking about some big names of the line, Asmodeus, Abbadon, Dagon &amp; Belial are the leaders of the Earthbounds. Lucifer? He's all over the gameline. I know because I ran it for years and it has always been great.<br /> <br /> Hopefully we'll soon get that Translation Guide. I mean, I don't mind flipping from CWoD to NWoD at all, but I can see while some would like to have some more &quot;classical&quot; Demons as playable characters in the NWoD setting. Personally, I love Descent as well and I appreciate that it is its own different, yet still intriguing, being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 09-16-2014, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T21:44:25-07:00","id":258683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=255339#post255339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of good stuff in there. Almost too much to talk about.<br /> <br /> I'm excited about Giants In The Earth, I'm amused by the SOE, and indifferent towards the apocalypse scenario. And on that note, I wonder if we'll ever get a second Infinite Macabre.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the Giants in The Earth too, it has tons of potential. Now it's ironic, as my Demon game has a sort of SOE already in the form of a Hunter Conspiracy of cybernetic humans ( think of a sort of fusion of Utopia Now with a bit of Cheiron Thaumatech madscience)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T08:18:56-07:00","id":259782,"title":"","content":"Copy pasting what I said on the actual blog page so prepare for a wall of text.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">I have to say this book sounds absolutely amazing. I love the Shards and the attention given to Angels, also a Crossover section is always nice to have. Happy to get more on the Exiles as well. And the chapter on Hell\u2019s is something I kinda missed in the Core so I cannot really express how excited I am to finally get it. A whole chapter focusing on the Cipher is also nice as creating a bunch of these for each game makes for a lot of workload for the ST, also hopefully it gives us something more about the Final Truth other than it is a line from a fortune cookie.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Now as for my concerns.<br /> <br /> Angel Chapter will suffer a bit in my opinion from the fact that it is done purely from an NPC standpoint. Also it might suffer a bit from the existing rules on Angels but that is neither here nor there as some things were set down long before this. Most of the time any splat done from purely NPC point of view ends up a bit bland and weak on actual substance, leaving them to look more like a monster of the week than interesting antagonists or influences that could be used long term. In most games these sort of NPC only splats end up as cardboard enemies and PC splats tend to get to be the long term real Antagonists.<br /> So to put it shortly a bit more PC flair on them would be nice.<br /> This also extends heavily to Exiles whom are done mostly through Angelic rules if I understood correctly and they should, in my humble opinion, be an PC splat instead of being NPC\u2019s only.<br /> Demon the Fallen for cWoD used to have complete rules for creating Earthbound as PC\u2019s even though they were Tormented alien mindsetted creatures more reminiscent of Cthulhu Mythos than anything else so I would think it wouldn\u2019t be unreasonable to have Exiles as PC\u2019s or even Angels for that matter. Being able to start from Angel PC\u2019s and playing through the Fall into their Descent and perhaps even finding Hell would be rather awesome after all.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Crossover Chapter is nice to have but this sounds absolutely horrid to my ears \u201cGive us these concepts as if they were part of the Demon line from day one. Don\u2019t make them unrecognizable, but cast them in the light of Descent rather than trying to negotiate crossover mechanics on even terms.\u201d Why? Because it suggest that these \u201cCrossover\u201d rules do not help me one bit in integrating these other lines into my DtD game since they are not actual crossover rules but rather conversions of certain beings into DtD line\u2019s mechanics. The other lines do not need a new Demon styled paint jobs but some actual Crossover rules could be helpful. And yes usually crossovers can be done by winging it but since we are getting a Crossover Chapter it would be nice to have it be of some use so that one wouldn\u2019t need to do it in the same improvisational style as in cWoD.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">That it for most of my concerns so I\u2019ll end this with a more happy note.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Giants in the Earth Shard sounds beyond awesome. Not only an historical setting but a historical setting with world shattering, or at least trembling, power. And the best thing is that from the looks of it Demons, Angels and the God-Machine all keep their sci-fi tech looks, judging from the comment that GM uses nuclear power etc.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T08:53:14-07:00","id":259789,"title":"","content":"You know how Hunter provided all those rules about how to present the other game lines without having to go and buy all those books?<br /> <br /> Same principle for DSG: Mechanically using Demon and basic WoD to portray those races so you don't have to go buy eight other books. Plus the perspective thing reflects that-when all you seee is angels and machines, everything looks like a holy gear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T09:35:00-07:00","id":259811,"title":"","content":"I recall reading that becoming an Exile is a tangible goal for Integrators, so if we could get something on that (mechanics would be nice, but I'm not holding my breath) that would be grand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T10:04:14-07:00","id":259819,"title":"","content":"I don't think they would be described in the detail in the Storyteller's Guide, but a book with at least a proper chapter (or the whole book itself) about the Exiles would be pretty sweet.<br /> <br /> They're that kind of &quot;not the most common yet still immensely useful and cool source of plot hooks&quot; NPCs that the NWoD had a lot of success by detailing in latter sourcebooks, like Bale Hounds, Banishers, Belial's Brood and (I'm already sure) the Mummy's Sixth Guild, just to name some.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T22:37:24-07:00","id":260373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=259789#post259789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how Hunter provided all those rules about how to present the other game lines without having to go and buy all those books?<br /> <br /> Same principle for DSG: Mechanically using Demon and basic WoD to portray those races so you don't have to go buy eight other books. Plus the perspective thing reflects that-when all you seee is angels and machines, everything looks like a holy gear.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kinda monstrosity belongs in the monster of the week chapter not crossover chapter as it is actually completely useless in a crossover situation. When dealing with an actual crossover situation having an other set of rules for portraying something similar to what you are playing is not only unhelpful but conflict creating at worst, when people start arguing about idiocy like Demon Vampires being different than requiem vampires etc.<br /> <br /> It's like in the cWoD there used to be, and still is, and antagonist chapter in each core that gives each main gamelines supernaturals in that games terms, that is in Vampire Core Mages use disciplines etc. This simple act, meant to give new ST's and those not interested in buying a complete new line to still use these supernaturals as NPC's, caused, and still causes, endless arguments about how the Lupines (werewolves) of Vampire are different from Garou (Werewolves of Werewolf) even though in pretty much each supplement described the same tribes for lupines that the Garou had etc. Do we need this kind of pointless arguments in nWoD? Beast is coming out designed to be crossover friendly so shouldn't we finally step out of the one-game-on-game-line line of thought into a more wider and complete world?<br /> <br /> For a chapter called out to be Crossover Chapter we should get some actual crossover material instead of muddying the waters even more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T06:43:34-07:00","id":260580,"title":"","content":"On the matter of the crossover chapter, I got the impression that its was going to be less &quot;Hunter&quot; and more &quot;Changeling/Geist&quot; with its fluff.<br /> <br /> That statements not very self-explanatory to, too expand the point. <br /> <br /> Take Werewolves.<br /> <br /> In the Hunter core we get a little info on Werewolves and what Hunters in general think about them. With more specific info being mentioned in each Compact/Conspiracy depending on how highly they value Werewolves as prey. Then Spirit Slayers expands all this stuff out.<br /> <br /> In Changeling both Rites of Spring and Equinox Road talk about Werewolves (and they have a couple of paragraphs in the core, but that's almost all basic crunch, so lets ignore it for this examples purposes). Both give *possible* Changeling views on Werewolves. However, as anyone who looks at the two game lines knows the two don't have a whole lot to do with one another and don't crossover as well as say... Changeling and Mage due to possible common elements. So unsurprisingly the Changelings &quot;fluff&quot; for Werewolves misses out the Spirit stuff, the duty too two worlds thing etc. It does engage with a &quot;Fae&quot; idea of what a Werewolf might be from the &quot;metaphysical opinionated/hamstrung&quot; viewpoint that Changelings often live in.<br /> <br /> The same books then go on into some reasonably crunch e.g. Spirits that enter the hedge automatically manifest, Luna has basically no sway there so Lunes can't enter it I believe. This could be considered the only &quot;objective&quot; crossover section.<br /> <br /> A similar thing was done in Book of the Dead when explaining how all the different splats at the time interact with entering, moving though and surviving in the Underworld. Most of the sections were &quot;point of view&quot; talk from the different splats about the Underworld, followed by a couple paragraphs of objective rules stuff.<br /> <br /> What I took from the outline for the ST guide is that its following the Book of the Dead of Equinox Road sorta build. In that it will have &quot;point of view&quot; fluff on the other splats from Demons. These will be &quot;wrong&quot; in the objective sense of the other game lines. They will include interesting ideas and plot hooks and ST can use if they want. Maybe there will be some general rules stuff e.g. what happens to a Demon in the Hedge? <br /> <br /> Later in the crossover chapter you'll actually get more crunch, but from a Demoncentric side when the &quot;embeds designed to deal with other Supernaturals&quot; are discussed on presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T08:14:15-07:00","id":260605,"title":"","content":"Haw said most of what I would, so I'll only add this:<br /> <br /> Muddying the waters is kind of a thing for horror settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T09:15:14-07:00","id":260630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=260605#post260605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haw said most of what I would, so I'll only add this:<br /> <br /> Muddying the waters is kind of a thing for horror settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it may work for fluff in a horror setting it sure as hell doesn't work for crunch in a game, even a horror game. Muddying the waters of fluff is ok, generally, while muddying the waters of crunch is just bad form and poor game design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T09:35:42-07:00","id":260679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=260630#post260630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it may work for fluff in a horror setting it sure as hell doesn't work for crunch in a game, even a horror game. Muddying the waters of fluff is ok, generally, while muddying the waters of crunch is just bad form and poor game design.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with this sentiment. However, non the examples I give do in fact do muddy the &quot;waters of crunch&quot; (good phrase). They muddy fluff and (usually) clarify crunch in a reasonable way. Hence why I have no worries (well little worry) about the Crossover section.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm more worried about the Angel chapter. Angels have flim-flammed in the fluff and crunch between being big-bad unstoppable Agent (Matrix analogy) like menaces to laughably minor villains that can could never threaten a Demon with a bit of XP. Its not a huge issue, as the base &quot;toolkit&quot; of the ephemeral creatures lets you custom up exceedingly dangerous Angels, but I'd like a bit more of a default tone for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T11:08:29-07:00","id":260776,"title":"","content":"Imagine you found this cool game. It's about techgnostic demons. You really like it, and wish you could see more of the world they have. You find out that there is, indeed, a whole new world behind them, full of faeries and vampires and wizards and what have you. But those core books, they cost a lot. You might be able to buy supplements, but to go through and buy all that will take a lot of saving. And you want to use this stuff now.<br /> <br /> Enter DSG. It gives a quick rundown with context you understand and provides rules to portray these things you deal with using the lexicon and powers you're used to. It's quick and dirty, but it lets you run the entire WoD on your limited scope.<br /> <br /> I imagine something like this is the thought behind the crossover chapter. Which isn't to say it won't be useful to those of us who own all the core books at least, but the idea as I understand Rose to be saying covers the bases better.<br /> <br /> Always gotta keep an eye on the potentially new guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T13:14:59-07:00","id":260920,"title":"","content":"I agree that the new guys need some simplified rules but if they are to be given such rules they belong into Antagonist/Monster of the Week/Urban Legends Chapter not the Crossover chapter which should be, you know, about actual Crossovers. If we are given a Crossover Chapter it should deal with actual crossovers, you know players playing different splats, not your average NPC builds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T20:18:05-07:00","id":261080,"title":"","content":"I'm going to admit, I must be kind of blind, because I feel like what Rose is talking about is helping facilitate both. I don't think you feel like that.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna drop it and just wait to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T20:54:39-07:00","id":262634,"title":"","content":"The &quot;crossover chapter&quot; isn't for playing multiple splats in a single ring. It's not even really for rules, although a few may turn up there. I was using the term &quot;crossover&quot; to refer to setting elements from other lines appearing in <i>Demon</i>, not to refer to using player characters from multiple games together. There won't be rules for that in this book. It's also not a chapter of sample NPC builds, although, again, we might see a stat block. It's explicitly about using setting elements from other games in <i>Demon</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T20:57:09-07:00","id":262635,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the Clarity, about time we Covered this.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, I know, I'm a Wise-ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T21:44:37-07:00","id":262650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=262634#post262634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;crossover chapter&quot; isn't for playing multiple splats in a single ring. It's not even really for rules, although a few may turn up there. I was using the term &quot;crossover&quot; to refer to setting elements from other lines appearing in <i>Demon</i>, not to refer to using player characters from multiple games together. There won't be rules for that in this book. It's also not a chapter of sample NPC builds, although, again, we might see a stat block. It's explicitly about using setting elements from other games in <i>Demon</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's awesome. That's what I want out of the chapter. Hashing out rules, and what splat to use I can do on my own, it's seeing the setting elements talked about in a cross-over manner that interests me the most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T23:04:05-07:00","id":262681,"title":"","content":"Same here. As a storyteller it is important to me to understand how demons interact with other creatures and how their themes can be used in my chronicle. That's all we need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T00:36:21-07:00","id":267250,"title":"","content":"To me that is still less of a crossover, which is why I am agaisnt calling the chapter that, and more about Antagonist or about the world at large in general. For me at least Crossover means actual Crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T16:33:18-07:00","id":267750,"title":"","content":"It's unlikely we'll use the word &quot;crossover&quot; in the book, if that helps. It's not part of our usual vocabulary, and you'll notice it's not in the title of the chapter. Outlines aren't book text or ad copy -- they're memos to writers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T19:25:22-07:00","id":267862,"title":"","content":"I'd personally like to see a small segment perhaps on how to run the techgnostic themes and general God-Machine, Angel, Infrastructurey stuff in the other lines...<br /> <br /> I'd like to see how a Vamp, Uratha, Mage, Promethean, Lost, Bound or Mummy would take discovering that there is a God-Machine and Angels behind the scenes... Though perhaps that's more the purview of a 'Blue Book' rather than a Demon one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T21:50:12-07:00","id":268765,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest - I think that the 'crossover' chapter is going to simply be the least interesting chapter in the book. I'll be glad that it's there when I read the final product, I'm sure, but it is quite thoroughly the least important thing in the entire book in my mind.<br /> <br /> The Angels section is going to be lots of fun, I hope. The Demon Core, Flowers and Interface provide us with heaps of Angels to use out of some fairly simplistic/basic moulds and I hope that it is focusing a lot on motives and missions is really exciting. It's all well and good to have an Angel do things, but giving them the justification and drive is harder.<br /> <br /> The Cipher hopefully should be really fun too - it's definitely the hardest concept in Demon to grasp, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T07:28:13-07:00","id":269013,"title":"","content":"Has anything been mentioned about Qashmal yet for the Guide? Being as they're 'angels' and got a mention in the Core as scuffling with the G-M Angels, I'd be interested to see more on their interactions with the G-M's machinations... Though I'm sure I'm not the only one who thinks this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T08:22:08-07:00","id":269100,"title":"","content":"Odds are they'll get a mention in the crossover chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T14:21:29-07:00","id":272492,"title":"","content":"Personally, I love when storyteller books go into depth how different supernatural creatures interact -- not only is it fun to read, but it gives you good insight into both supernatural types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T15:00:25-07:00","id":272511,"title":"","content":"Yeah but then they could just make the big book of crossover and be finished with it. I just got Seattle and skipped over that inane section. I mean there core books for every splat pick then up if you want info on them but wasting precious word count on more cross over is disheartening. But from my read of Roses explanation it sounds more thematic than anything. It could be bearable if there is no tirade about how demons interact with the covenants but more how angencies can be presented like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T09:27:58-07:00","id":559478,"title":"","content":"Not to drag up the past, but it's made it to Development! Hopefully its in there only a short time and I can get my hands on some Demon-y, Demon-y goodness soon. I've been reading up a lot on ancient history and have been actually working to improve my Biblical History, so I'm really looking forward to the Biblical setting. It wil be very neat!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T00:25:19-07:00","id":560504,"title":"","content":"I know this is a months-old post, but I really want to comment that miss_minty's perspective on the Seattle book and its crossover section is utterly bewildering to me, because it amounts to &quot;I really hate that this nWoD setting book is an nWoD setting book.&quot; Although, like most setting books, it's focused primarily on a single splat that's especially prominent in that particular locale, it's kind of a fundamental failing of a book that's supposed to be providing a setting for the nWoD to <b>not</b> provide at least nominal coverage of what's going on there with the other splats, as well as a disservice to anyone who wants to involve that locale in their non-Demon games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2836-nezumi","name":"Nezumi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T15:08:50-07:00","id":561260,"title":"","content":"Because Demon has had crossover ideas since it's corebook, it makes sense that a book might cover other splats in the area, but it's in no way required. In the same way that City of the Damned: New Orleans doesn't really need to get into other splats because it's a Vampire supplement, or Boston Unveiled doesn't need to get into other supernaturals, because it's a Mage supplement. That they choose to do so in the book for Seattle is nice and likely a consequence of Matt's enjoyment of Crossover, but it's definitely not required, and the fully realized setting of <i>Demon: The Descent </i>doesn't really suffer from the absence of the other splats.<br /> <br /> It's not an unreasonable perspective, just one with which you disagree. Now, if this was a Beast setting book, it might actually <i>require </i>that sort of info, but Demon doesn't <i>need </i>it really. It's still cool, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T23:11:36-07:00","id":561616,"title":"","content":"Wait, are you saying other setting books <b>didn't</b> have at least nominal coverage of other splats? (I never had any before, because the lines I was most interested didn't have individual setting books, and mostly came out after Chicago) That's... disappointing. I generally prefer the assumption that, even if they don't appear in a given chronicle, everything else in the nWoD still <b>exists</b>, and a book that effectively treats nothing but, say, vampires as existing in a given location feels less &quot;real&quot; to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2836-nezumi","name":"Nezumi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T05:33:57-07:00","id":561807,"title":"","content":"I must say, Boston Unveiled do not assume that Vampires and Werewolves do not exist, but it does assume that there aren't that many in the city proper, or that they at least hide pretty well. According to the book, most Vampire activity is in the Fens (parkland and urban wild), and most Werewolves keep to rural Massachusetts to the east of Boston. The main reason for Vampires keeping out or low profile seems to be Banishers hunting them, as it is hard to protect yourself against that without Mage support. Werewolves stay away because the spirit courts of the city are pretty werewolf unfriendly, having risen to power with Mage support.<br /> <br /> On the other side, the New Orleans book is the worst for crossover, because while it explicitly assumes the Werewolf and Mage populations to be low to non-existent, it does not give any reasons for that. But I believe all other city/setting books either give info on what other supernaturals are up to, or plausible reasons why they keep out, just like Boston does.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Technically, Hunting Grounds: the Rockies also has no information on Mages (but it has info on vampires). I guess this is mostly because it was released before the Mage Rulebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":". 06-20-2015, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:28:41-07:00","id":566723,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the \u201cBiblical era shard\u201d appears to be \u201cthe Unchained vs. the God-Machine in the ancient Middle East\u201d, <i>not</i> \u201chow to recast DtD as Biblical demons rebelling against the Biblical God\u201d. In effect, it appears to be not so much a Shard as a Dark Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:38:25-07:00","id":566731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=566723#post566723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that the \u201cBiblical era shard\u201d appears to be \u201cthe Unchained vs. the God-Machine in the ancient Middle East\u201d, <i>not</i> \u201chow to recast DtD as Biblical demons rebelling against the Biblical God\u201d. In effect, it appears to be not so much a Shard as a Dark Era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, and it will be glorious! What it is a shard of though is how to do a low tech Demon game. Or at least, that's what I expect it will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:41:19-07:00","id":566746,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping for a good mix of anachronism. Hypertech heavens hidden under clay buildings and an agricultural revolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T18:51:12-08:00","id":804186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/255162-has-everyone-checked-out-the-demon-storytellers-guide-outline?p=566731#post566731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup, and it will be glorious! What it is a shard of though is how to do a low tech Demon game. Or at least, that's what I expect it will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read that shard. You can use high-tech devices in areas that the God Machine controls but need to pay a thematically resonant price from your resources to KEEP using them. It's a literal arm and a leg for your new car! And the tech is not user-friendly so keep an eye on that rebellious toaster! Everything outside is normal tech. It's not as useful as what the god machine makes but you know that it's safe to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":885,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","user":"bwgustaf","date":". 01-08-2016, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T19:52:45-08:00","id":804223,"title":"","content":"So apparently anyone that steals tech from the God Machine becomes Stigmatic. I read a passage in the Book of Joshua where the leaders are trying to figure out which spy took something valuable from Jerchico after God himself said not to take any spoils... Combining the 2 in an ambiguous way could make for a really exciting adventure hook!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}